ts, embracing Väli, went round him, with tears trickling from her eyes.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-16-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4016009","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"080f7b23693c0872d6686554ba43ab076c71f8dcae5ac3c44486372150e8f8a8","compact":"59b8c062077e38523cdda62e71041d8bc3f9ab67151a371d21df9134575297f6","nasal":"977e710abe604036ac9da5e920a57470ed217890530ffff2914b8a1afe72aa53"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-16-10","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":16,"verse":10,"english":"Having performed Sastayana or the ceremony of benediction, that one gifted with a knowledge of Mantras, and desirous of Vāli's success, went, overwhelmed with grief, to the inner-apartment in the company of other females.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.899,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-16-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4016010","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3777daae6067bbd8562e8bc32f01c9c3b2f3cd8327b3ad552e9311064be0d1b3","compact":"f17f6d8dfecb40c1801550b9a70868f40ce3d4e751c583c1da44f9cb238c6b11","nasal":"3eb9202efb3c86cc3901d578ef8d423f9721ce69964558ca5ce2dd7d82d52e7e"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-16-11","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":16,"verse":11,"english":"After Tārā had departed to her own quarters with her female companions, he issued out of the city sighing like an enraged serpent.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-16-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4016011","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"21f0d1436fa94c54a9c01a2bb1782ff289bf74a63badc604e60780d4f6e3b96a","compact":"165ef3406f9e349aea96cb0e7f6ae1baa88218e0c737dc904e041203bb34a1aa","nasal":"27ea41a